# valgrind suppressions for the constant-time check (ct_check.c).
#
# There is exactly one: Monocypher's crypto_aead_read() branches on the
# result of crypto_verify16() to decide whether to decrypt. That result (tag
# right or wrong) is public by design; the comparison that produces it is
# constant time and is checked separately. monocypher.c is compiled with
# -fno-inline for this check, so crypto_aead_read's own body contains no
# other conditional than that one (its loops run over public lengths, and
# everything else is a call into a separate function, which is checked).
{
   monocypher-aead-read-declassifies-tag-check
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:crypto_aead_read
}
